    {
      "id": 141173,
      "name": "Theta_Sigma",
      "username": "Theta_Sigma",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/theta_sigma/{size}/1929_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-06-10T16:00:51.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"cmschex\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/e9bcb4/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> cmschex:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>All I am reminded of is the Avatar the Last Airbender episode where they introduce Toph, who is fighting in that world's version of UFC. &nbsp;There is a fighter called The Boulder (who is an obvious parody of The Rock) who only refers to himself as \"The Boulder\" in every sentance. &nbsp;Now I need to get back to work on my A:TLA customr Sentinels decks…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I went back up and reread SIlverleaf's post, but imagined her growling 'The SIlverleaf' the way The Boulder growled his name in his appearances.</p>",
      "post_number": 11,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:18:13.575Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
